      "id": "GENUS_BALEARICA",
      "name": "Balearica",
      "rank": "GENUS",
      "description": "Crowned cranes — the most ancient crane lineage, distinguished by their stiff golden crest of wiry feathers atop the head and their ability to perch in trees, a behaviour unique among cranes. They inhabit African savanna wetlands and grasslands. The display of a crowned crane — bowing, leaping, and calling with its inflatable red throat pouch — is one of the most elaborate in the bird world.",
      "lineage": "Palearctic Cranes",
